<div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackfox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1271391-scion-2e-kickstarter-update-67-atlantis?p=1271408#post1271408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really liked these primordials. Also Amnis and Badarus are coming back! I can't wait to see the rest of the atlantean pantheon on this edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are these two Primordials? It mentions that the two Incarnate into the World, which Primordials don't really do because they're too darn big.<br /> <br /> Eh, semantics, I suppose","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T14:43:38-08:00","id":1271589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1271391-scion-2e-kickstarter-update-67-atlantis?p=1271581#post1271581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are these two Primordials? It mentions that the two Incarnate into the World, which Primordials don't really do because they're too darn big.<br /> <br /> Eh, semantics, I suppose</div> </div> </div> </div>My interpretation is they originate as Primordials as the creators of the cosmos, but they became Gods by incarnating themselves into the World.<br /> <br /> (The Trimurti did the same thing)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-05T08:25:16-08:00","id":1278821,"title":"","content":"We already know the callings for Aeva and Ytar, but I've been wondering what callings the other gods will get. These are my guesses for the ones that are &quot;confirmed&quot; to come back:<br /> <br /> Amnis: Guardian, Healer, Sage<br /> <br /> Badarus: Leader, Liminal, Sage<br /> <br /> I'm so hyped for these atlanteans hahaha I just hope the other five are brought back as well","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24802-blackfox","user":"Blackfox","date":". 01-05-2019, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24802-blackfox","name":"Blackfox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}